{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GD4YSqkkdK5dF7wthx8X6y","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd104-test\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/test: Evaluate Conditional Expressions\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  macOS ships test (and [) but the GNU version has specific behavior for multi-argument\n6\t  expressions and parenthesized groups. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU\n7\t  reference binary (gtest, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations,\n8\t  verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n9\t\n10\tgoals:\n11\t  - G1: Evaluate conditional expressions and exit with status 0 (true) or 1 (false).\n12\t  - G2: Support file tests, string tests, and integer comparisons.\n13\t  - G3: Support logical operators (-a, -o, !) and parenthesized groups.\n14\t  - G4: Verify functional parity against gtest via differential testing.\n15\t\n16\trequirements:\n17\t  R1:\n18\t    title: File tests\n19\t    items:\n20\t      - R1.1:\n21\t          text: \"Must support file test operators: -e (exists), -f (regular file), -d (directory), -s (non-empty), -r (readable), -w (writable), -x (executable), -L or -h (symlink), -b (block special), -c (character special), -p (named pipe), -S (socket), -g (setgid), -u (setuid), -k (sticky), -G (owned by effective GID), -O (owned by effective UID), -t FD (terminal).\"\n22\t      - R1.2:\n23\t          text: \"Must support file comparison operators: FILE1 -nt FILE2 (newer than), FILE1 -ot FILE2 (older than), FILE1 -ef FILE2 (same device and inode).\"\n24\t\n25\t  R2:\n26\t    title: String and integer tests\n27\t    items:\n28\t      - R2.1:\n29\t          text: \"Must support string operators: -z STRING (zero length), -n STRING (non-zero length), STRING1 = STRING2 (equal), STRING1 != STRING2 (not equal), STRING (non-empty).\"\n30\t      - R2.2:\n31\t          text: \"Must support integer comparison operators: INT1 -eq INT2, -ne, -lt, -le, -gt, -ge.\"\n32\t\n33\t  R3:\n34\t    title: Logical operators\n35\t    items:\n36\t      - R3.1:\n37\t          text: \"Must support logical operators: ! EXPR (not), EXPR1 -a EXPR2 (and), EXPR1 -o EXPR2 (or), ( EXPR ) (grouping). Parentheses must be escaped or quoted by the shell.\"\n38\t      - R3.2:\n39\t          text: Must exit 0 when the expression evaluates to true, 1 when false, and 2 on syntax errors.\n40\t\n41\t  R4:\n42\t    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n43\t    items:\n44\t      - R4.1:\n45\t          text: Must exit 0 (true), 1 (false), or 2 (error).\n46\t      - R4.2:\n47\t          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n48\t\n49\tnon_goals:\n50\t  - cmd/test does not implement == (use = for string equality, matching POSIX).\n51\t  - cmd/test does not implement regex matching (=~).\n52\t\n53\tacceptance_criteria:\n54\t  - id: AC1\n55\t    criterion: \"test -f /etc/passwd exits 0, matching gtest.\"\n56\t    traces:\n57\t      - R1.1\n58\t  - id: AC2\n59\t    criterion: \"test 1 -eq 1 exits 0, test 1 -eq 2 exits 1, matching gtest.\"\n60\t    traces:\n61\t      - R2.2\n62\t  - id: AC3\n63\t    criterion: \"test ! -d /nonexistent exits 0, matching gtest.\"\n64\t    traces:\n65\t      - R3.1\n66\t  - id: AC4\n67\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gtest passes.\"\n68\t    traces:\n69\t      - R1.1\n70\t      - R2.1\n71\t      - R2.2\n72\t      - R3.1\n73\t  - id: AC5\n74\t    criterion: \"cmd/test compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n75\t    traces:\n76\t      - R1.1\n77\t      - R1.2\n78\t      - R2.1\n79\t      - R2.2\n80\t      - R3.1\n81\t      - R3.2\n82\t      - R4.1\n83\t      - R4.2\n84\t\n85\tpackage_contract:\n86\t  imports:\n87\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n88\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed8c8e34-76dc-4cfa-889a-85c07d83f684","uuid":"18d56b58-61a6-466c-851a-d2ba13696c94","timestamp":"2026-05-27T15:54:25.916Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5603/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd104-test.yaml","content":"id: srd104-test\ntitle: \"cmd/test: Evaluate Conditional Expressions\"\n\nproblem: |\n  macOS ships test (and [) but the GNU version has specific behavior for multi-argument\n  expressions and parenthesized groups. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU\n  reference binary (gtest, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations,\n  verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Evaluate conditional expressions and exit with status 0 (true) or 1 (false).\n  - G2: Support file tests, string tests, and integer comparisons.\n  - G3: Support logical operators (-a, -o, !) and parenthesized groups.\n  - G4: Verify functional parity against gtest via differential testing.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: File tests\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: \"Must support file test operators: -e (exists), -f (regular file), -d (directory), -s (non-empty), -r (readable), -w (writable), -x (executable), -L or -h (symlink), -b (block special), -c (character special), -p (named pipe), -S (socket), -g (setgid), -u (setuid), -k (sticky), -G (owned by effective GID), -O (owned by effective UID), -t FD (terminal).\"\n      - R1.2:\n          text: \"Must support file comparison operators: FILE1 -nt FILE2 (newer than), FILE1 -ot FILE2 (older than), FILE1 -ef FILE2 (same device and inode).\"\n\n  R2:\n    title: String and integer tests\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: \"Must support string operators: -z STRING (zero length), -n STRING (non-zero length), STRING1 = STRING2 (equal), STRING1 != STRING2 (not equal), STRING (non-empty).\"\n      - R2.2:\n          text: \"Must support integer comparison operators: INT1 -eq INT2, -ne, -lt, -le, -gt, -ge.\"\n\n  R3:\n    title: Logical operators\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: \"Must support logical operators: ! EXPR (not), EXPR1 -a EXPR2 (and), EXPR1 -o EXPR2 (or), ( EXPR ) (grouping). Parentheses must be escaped or quoted by the shell.\"\n      - R3.2:\n          text: Must exit 0 when the expression evaluates to true, 1 when false, and 2 on syntax errors.\n\n  R4:\n    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n    items:\n      - R4.1:\n          text: Must exit 0 (true), 1 (false), or 2 (error).\n      - R4.2:\n          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/test does not implement == (use = for string equality, matching POSIX).\n  - cmd/test does not implement regex matching (=~).\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"test -f /etc/passwd exits 0, matching gtest.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"test 1 -eq 1 exits 0, test 1 -eq 2 exits 1, matching gtest.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.2\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"test ! -d /nonexistent exits 0, matching gtest.\"\n    traces:\n      - R3.1\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gtest passes.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R3.1\n  - id: AC5\n    criterion: \"cmd/test compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n\npackage_contract:\n  imports:\n    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n","numLines":88,"startLine":1,"totalLines":88}}}
