{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via cobbler orchestrator) assigned task #5603: implement srd104-test requirements R3.1, R3.2, R4.1, R4.2 in `cmd/test/main.go`. This extends an existing `test` command implementation (which already has R1.1, R1.2, R2.1, R2.2 from a prior task) with:\n   - **R3.1**: Logical operators: `! EXPR` (not), `EXPR1 -a EXPR2` (and), `EXPR1 -o EXPR2` (or), `( EXPR )` (grouping)\n   - **R3.2**: Exit 0 when true, 1 when false, 2 on syntax errors\n   - **R4.1**: Exit codes 0 (true), 1 (false), 2 (error)\n   - **R4.2**: SIGPIPE handling via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler`\n\n   Acceptance criteria: compiles without errors, `go vet` clean, all R3.1/R3.2/R4.1/R4.2 behavior implemented, existing R1.x/R2.x behavior preserved.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Recursive descent parser for conditional expressions with operator precedence\n   - GNU `test` / `[` command semantics (POSIX conditional expressions)\n   - Operator precedence: `-o` (lowest) < `-a` < `!` < primary (unary/binary/parenthesized)\n   - Differential testing against GNU reference binary `gtest`\n   - SIGPIPE handler pattern via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Exit code conventions: 0=true, 1=false, 2=error\n   - Non-goals: no `==` (use `=`), no regex matching (`=~`)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **`docs/specs/software-requirements/srd104-test.yaml`** (read, full SRD):\n     - Defines all requirements R1-R4 for the test command\n     - R3.1: logical operators `!`, `-a`, `-o`, `( )`\n     - R3.2: exit codes 0/1/2\n     - R4.1: exit codes 0/1/2 (overlaps R3.2)\n     - R4.2: SIGPIPE handling\n     - Non-goals: no `==`, no `=~`\n\n   - **`cmd/test/main.go`** (read, existing 270-line implementation):\n     - Already implements R1.1 (file test operators), R1.2 (file comparison), R2.1 (string ops), R2.2 (integer comparisons)\n     - Has `parser` struct with `args []string`, `pos int`\n     - Helper methods: `peek()`, `advance()`, `remaining()`\n     - **Current `expr()` just calls `primary()` directly — NO logical operator support**:\n       ```go\n       func (p *parser) expr() bool {\n           return p.primary()\n       }\n       ```\n     - `primary()` handles: binary ops (3-arg lookahead), unary ops, bare string test\n     - `exitError()` already exits with code 2\n     - `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` already called at line 19 (R4.2 done)\n     - Main already exits 0/1 based on result (lines 41-44)\n     - `isUnaryOp()` recognizes all file/string unary operators\n     - `isBinaryOp()` recognizes `=`, `!=`, `-eq`/`-ne`/`-lt`/`-le`/`-gt`/`-ge`, `-nt`/`-ot`/`-ef`\n     - `evalUnary()` dispatches to string tests, `-t` terminal test, access tests, and `fileStatTest()`\n     - `evalBinary()` dispatches to string comparison, `intCompare()`, `fileCompare()`\n     - Full existing code is 270 lines\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet — only file reads were performed before the summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified that R4.2 (SIGPIPE) is already implemented in the existing code\n   - Identified that R4.1 and R3.2 (exit codes) are already partially implemented — `exitError()` exits 2, main exits 0/1\n   - The main gap is R3.1: the `expr()` method needs to become a proper recursive descent parser with `-o`, `-a`, `!`, and `( )` support\n   - The `primary()` method needs `(` `)` grouping support added\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: Massive task prompt from cobbler orchestrator containing: role definition, repository file list, project context (VISION, ARCHITECTURE, SPECIFICATIONS, roadmap, analysis, requirement states), task description (#5603 — implement srd104 R3.1, R3.2, R4.1, R4.2), execution constitution, go style constitution, constraints, shared protocols, package contracts\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" — Instructed to provide a summary instead of continuing with tool calls.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Modify `cmd/test/main.go` to implement R3.1 (logical operators: `!`, `-a`, `-o`, `( )` grouping)\n   - Verify R3.2/R4.1 exit code behavior is complete\n   - Verify R4.2 SIGPIPE is already handled (it is)\n   - Run `go build -o bin/test ./cmd/test/` to verify compilation\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/test/...` to verify no issues\n   - Ensure existing R1.x/R2.x behavior is preserved\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just read the SRD (`srd104-test.yaml`) and the existing implementation (`cmd/test/main.go`). I was about to plan and implement the changes to add logical operator support to the recursive descent parser. The key change needed is transforming the parser's `expr()` method from a simple `primary()` call into a proper precedence-climbing parser:\n\n   - `expr()` → parse `-o` (OR) chains\n   - New `andExpr()` → parse `-a` (AND) chains  \n   - New `notExpr()` → parse `!` prefix\n   - Modify `primary()` → add `( EXPR )` grouping support before existing unary/binary/bare-string logic\n\n   The existing `primary()` logic for unary ops, binary ops, and bare strings must be preserved intact.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write the modified `cmd/test/main.go` with the recursive descent parser extended for R3.1 logical operators. The specific changes:\n   \n   1. Rewrite `expr()` to handle `-o`:\n      ```go\n      func (p *parser) expr() bool {\n          result := p.andExpr()\n          for p.peek() == \"-o\" {\n              p.advance()\n              right := p.andExpr()\n              result = result || right\n          }\n          return result\n      }\n      ```\n   \n   2. Add `andExpr()` for `-a`:\n      ```go\n      func (p *parser) andExpr() bool {\n          result := p.notExpr()\n          for p.peek() == \"-a\" {\n              p.advance()\n